  "difficulty_level": "H1",
  "difficulty_reason": "This unrestricted scalar-extension theorem for maximal weakly etale subalgebras requires more than finite separable tensor-product formulas: the proof passes through arbitrary filtered algebras, nilpotent reduction, total quotient rings and finite products, then identifies the separable constant field of a finitely generated field using geometric irreducibility over an algebraic closure. The retained weakly-etale classification and maximal-subalgebra construction make this an advanced non-Noetherian structural base-change result.",
